   "title": "Read me",
   "properties": {},
   "widgets_values": [
    "## Idol · one image to a 3D Gaussian splat\n\n[Idol](https://github.com/speridlabs/idol-sdk) by speridlabs turns one picture of an object into up to a million 3D Gaussians, including the sides the picture never showed. It is TripoSplat's architecture with its own weights, so it runs on ComfyUI's native TripoSplat nodes; the [ComfyUI-Idol](https://github.com/PedroMarinhoDev/ComfyUI-Idol) pack adds **Idol Preprocess Image** (Idol's crop, with its mode for photos), **Idol Input Camera** (the input's viewpoint, which Idol predicts) and **Idol Precision**.\n\n**Model files** (each loader links its file, so ComfyUI offers to download what's missing)\n\n| File | Folder |\n|---|---|\n| [idol_fp32.safetensors](https://huggingface.co/PedroMarinhoDev/Idol-ComfyUI/blob/main/diffusion_models/idol_fp32.safetensors) | `models/diffusion_models` |\n| [idol_vae_decoder_fp32.safetensors](https://huggingface.co/PedroMarinhoDev/Idol-ComfyUI/blob/main/vae/idol_vae_decoder_fp32.safetensors) | `models/vae` |\n| [dino_v3_vit_h.safetensors](https://huggingface.co/VAST-AI/TripoSplat/blob/main/clip_vision/dino_v3_vit_h.safetensors) | `models/clip_vision` |\n| [flux2-vae.safetensors](https://huggingface.co/VAST-AI/TripoSplat/blob/main/vae/flux2-vae.safetensors) | `models/vae` |\n| [birefnet.safetensors](https://huggingface.co/Comfy-Org/BiRefNet/blob/main/background_removal/birefnet.safetensors) | `models/background_removal` |\n\n**Settings are Idol's:** euler, scheduler simple, 50 steps, **cfg 4** (Idol's guidance 3 in ComfyUI's convention); the time shift 3 is built into the model. Use the same **mode** on both Idol nodes: synthetic for renders and generated images, real for photos.\n\n**Background:** an image with transparency can skip Remove Background: connect Load Image's MASK through an Invert Mask node instead.\n\n**Precision (Idol Precision):** default is fp16 on most GPUs, the precision the Idol SDK itself runs in: 24 s of sampling on an RTX 4090. **fp32** reproduces the full-precision model (colours within 0.01/255 of it, against 0.4/255 on average and 4/255 at worst for fp16), 112 s. **fp32, fp16 attention** is the middle: 0.05/255, 42 s. fp32 needs the fp32 file. Keep Idol Precision in the graph even at default: it patches ComfyUI's TripoSplat code, which otherwise runs an fp32 file in fp32 whatever you choose. The decoder computes in its file's dtype.\n\n**Outputs:** the .ply in output/3d, a render from the input's viewpoint, and a turntable video that starts there."
   ],
   "widgets_values_named": {
    "text": "## Idol · one image to a 3D Gaussian splat\n\n[Idol](https://github.com/speridlabs/idol-sdk) by speridlabs turns one picture of an object into up to a million 3D Gaussians, including the sides the picture never showed. It is TripoSplat's architecture with its own weights, so it runs on ComfyUI's native TripoSplat nodes; the [ComfyUI-Idol](https://github.com/PedroMarinhoDev/ComfyUI-Idol) pack adds **Idol Preprocess Image** (Idol's crop, with its mode for photos), **Idol Input Camera** (the input's viewpoint, which Idol predicts) and **Idol Precision**.\n\n**Model files** (each loader links its file, so ComfyUI offers to download what's missing)\n\n| File | Folder |\n|---|---|\n| [idol_fp32.safetensors](https://huggingface.co/PedroMarinhoDev/Idol-ComfyUI/blob/main/diffusion_models/idol_fp32.safetensors) | `models/diffusion_models` |\n| [idol_vae_decoder_fp32.safetensors](https://huggingface.co/PedroMarinhoDev/Idol-ComfyUI/blob/main/vae/idol_vae_decoder_fp32.safetensors) | `models/vae` |\n| [dino_v3_vit_h.safetensors](https://huggingface.co/VAST-AI/TripoSplat/blob/main/clip_vision/dino_v3_vit_h.safetensors) | `models/clip_vision` |\n| [flux2-vae.safetensors](https://huggingface.co/VAST-AI/TripoSplat/blob/main/vae/flux2-vae.safetensors) | `models/vae` |\n| [birefnet.safetensors](https://huggingface.co/Comfy-Org/BiRefNet/blob/main/background_removal/birefnet.safetensors) | `models/background_removal` |\n\n**Settings are Idol's:** euler, scheduler simple, 50 steps, **cfg 4** (Idol's guidance 3 in ComfyUI's convention); the time shift 3 is built into the model. Use the same **mode** on both Idol nodes: synthetic for renders and generated images, real for photos.\n\n**Background:** an image with transparency can skip Remove Background: connect Load Image's MASK through an Invert Mask node instead.\n\n**Precision (Idol Precision):** default is fp16 on most GPUs, the precision the Idol SDK itself runs in: 24 s of sampling on an RTX 4090. **fp32** reproduces the full-precision model (colours within 0.01/255 of it, against 0.4/255 on average and 4/255 at worst for fp16), 112 s. **fp32, fp16 attention** is the middle: 0.05/255, 42 s. fp32 needs the fp32 file. Keep Idol Precision in the graph even at default: it patches ComfyUI's TripoSplat code, which otherwise runs an fp32 file in fp32 whatever you choose. The decoder computes in its file's dtype.\n\n**Outputs:** the .ply in output/3d, a render from the input's viewpoint, and a turntable video that starts there."
   },
